{
  "positive_alignment_reasons": [
    "The Kettering Incident felt worth trying because its speculative mystery connects with what interested me about Star Trek: The Next Generation."
  ],
  "negative_misalignment_reasons": [
    "Rio Lobo did not fit because I am not looking for a Western right now; watching one kind of story does not mean I want any film or series.",
    "I could not connect the unidentified items to my interests, and The Bay's title alone gave me too little to decide whether its story would appeal to me."
  ],
  "overgeneralized_signals": [
    "My past viewing seems to have been taken as a broader interest in unrelated stories than I currently have.",
    "The popularity differences do not explain why I would enjoy these choices, so they give me no reason to choose them."
  ],
  "missing_or_underweighted_signals": [
    "The speculative aspect of my interest in Star Trek matters more to this choice than simply finding something else to watch.",
    "I choose selectively and need a recognizable connection to a story before I will try it; most of my history here does not reveal enough to establish that connection."
  ],
  "summary_diagnosis": "The Kettering Incident makes a plausible connection to my interest in speculative stories, but most other choices give me no clear reason to expect a match."
}"}
